## Lore

Mystic Knights are among the most hated and feared warriors on the continent:
merciless mercenaries, assassins, enforcers and killers who sell their services
to evil - Necromancers, the Splugorth, Lord Dunscon, the Grim Reapers, the
Society of Sages and the Black Market among them. Most common in the Magic
Zone, they are found across eastern North America and only occasionally in the
west or far north. They swear fealty to no nation and fight for money or
revenge, usually in pairs or groups of three to six. More than a dozen together
means a war or massacre is coming.

They are like evil Ronin with no honor. A client who hires one knows he is
unleashing a murderous, chaotic force and cannot hold the Knight to account for
the slaughter that follows. Erin Tarn recorded their creed as an assassin''s
code: the end justifies the means; know thy enemy; dead enemies tell no tales;
the weak are meant to be dominated; seize opportunity without regret; revenge
is sweet and best when it waits; respect the one who pays you until a new
master replaces him; and never betray the Eternal Order of the Mystic Knights,
their one true ally.

Also known as the "Death Knights."

## Magic

Being Mystics, their spell knowledge is intuitive. After years of pondering
life, three days of fasting and meditation - or of nonstop fighting and
bloodletting - leave the Knight knowing Magic Shield, Armor of Ithan, Aura of
Death, Tongues, Energize Spell, Fists of Fury and Power Weapon. At each later
level he meditates on combat, revenge and magic and gains two spells from
levels 1-6. He can never be taught or buy spells, but uses Techno-Wizard
devices and covets magic weapons and armor, especially rune weapons.

P.P.E.: 2D4x10 plus P.E., +2D6 per level, drawing twice the usual amount at
ley lines and nexus points.

## Psionics

A major psychic: See the Invisible, Sixth Sense, Resist Fatigue and Mind Block,
plus three Sensitive or Physical powers of choice. One more Sensitive or
Physical power per level from second, one Super power at fourth level and
another at ninth. I.S.P.: 5D6+6 plus M.E., +1D6+1 per additional level.

## Equipment and Money

Standard Mystic Knight body armor (70 M.D.C.) and a Demon-Ram helmet with
curled horns (50 M.D.C.), of M.D.C. composites or magically created material;
not a full environmental suit. Weapons: a magic sword, three ancient weapons of
choice (no special powers) and two modern weapons. A player character starts
without transportation; NPCs may have a horse, monster steed, hovercycle or
other vehicle, and NPC villains may carry more magic weapons and items.

Money: 2D4x1000 credits and 1D4x1000 worth of precious metals or gems. They
work as mercenaries, assassins and bounty hunters and are usually paid 50% to
100% more than others, for their reputation and powers.

## Player Characters

The book prints the Mystic Knight as an NPC villain and optional player
character, and does not suggest evil Mystic Knights for players: in a group of
mostly good characters, conflict and violence are likely. Race: none, though
most (60%) are human; men and women alike. A high I.Q., P.S., P.P. and M.E. are
useful but not required.

Rumour tells of the Order of the White Rose, heroic Mystic Knights of good,
aberrant and selfish alignments who betrayed their brethren to become
mercenaries for good. The Mystic Knights insist every one was hunted down and
killed; if they exist, they are few and secret.

## GM Notes

About 4000 Mystic Knights are believed to work in the Magic Zone (hundreds for
Lord Dunscon), with perhaps as many again across North America and Canada.
There are at least two enclaves in the Magic Zone and one near Free Quebec.
The Corrupt count them among their natural enemies (printed 88).
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'mystic-knight');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'mystic-knight';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-mystic-knight-class.sql');
